.TH MPROTECT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
mprotect \- change memory mapping protection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/mman.h>
.B int mprotect(void* address, size_t byte_count, int protection);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Changes protection for a mapped range beginning at a page\-aligned address.
Protection combines PROT_READ, PROT_WRITE and PROT_EXEC, or is PROT_NONE.
Invalid access to a protected mapping may deliver SIGSEGV.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mmap (3crunch),
.BR mprotect (2)
